INSTRUCTOR OR ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF NURSING Employment Apply Now Menu Administrative Openings Digital Marketing Specialist Administrative Assistant to the Business and Nursing Departments Administrative Assistant to the President and Provost Administrative Computing Support Specialist Business Office/ HR Associate Development Officer Gift and Data Entry Assistant Institutional Research Reporter and Analyst IT Systems Administrator ITS Workstation Support Associate Residential Education Coordinator Residential Operations Coordinator Academic Openings ASSISTANT/ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR OF NURSING AND BSN PROGRAM DIRECTOR VISITING INSTRUCTOR OR ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF NURSING Contact or visit us Human Resources Smith-Curtis 202 5000 Saint Paul Avenue Lincoln, NE 68504 Fax (402) 465-2565 Employment Opportunity for the Position of VISITING INSTRUCTOR OR ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF NURSING Status The Nebraska Wesleyan University (NWU) Nursing Program has an opening for a full-time Visiting Instructor or Assistant Professor faculty position with a start date of August 17, 2026 (classes start August 25, 2026). This faculty member will primarily teach in the Pre-licensure BSN program. NWU may be posting a more permanent full-time position in Spring 2027. The visiting assistant professor would be encouraged to apply. Nebraska Wesleyan University is an independent Methodist liberal arts university of approximately 1,500 undergraduate and graduate students in Lincoln, Nebraska. The University’s steadfast commitment to putting learning into action through internships, service learning and collaborative research has yielded tremendous outcomes for students and alumni. NWU offers a competitive wage and comprehensive benefits plan including Health, Dental and Vision Insurance, Life Insurance, Disability benefits, and retirement benefits. Department Nursing Responsibilities * Teach undergraduate nursing courses. * Work with nursing faculty to plan, implement, and evaluate nursing curriculum, and related activities. Qualifications * A master's degree in nursing required; earned doctorate or near completion will be given preference * License to practice nursing in the state of Nebraska is required * Demonstrated commitment to student academic achievement * Demonstrated critical thinking and time management skills * Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with a variety of constituents * Demonstrated written and oral communication skills * Willingness to offer office hours or availability to students outside of scheduled lectures and labs Salary Competitive wage and comprehensive benefi ts plan including Health Insurance, Life Insurance,Disability benefi ts, Retirement, fi ve weeks of paid time off per year with vacation and holidays, and100% tuition discount for dependents after one year. How to Apply To apply, please upload a cover letter, resume or curriculum vita, and the names of three professional references at the following URL: https://nebrwesleyan.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . NWU encourages applicants to address how one or more of NWU’s Core Values align with their personal values and characteristics and/or how they would contribute to them at NWU in their cover letter or a separate document. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Nebraska Wesleyan University provides equal educational and employment opportunities to qualified persons in all areas of university operation without regard to religion or creed, age, genetic information, gender identity and expression, sexual identity and orientation, veteran status, disability, marital status, race, or national or ethnic origin, in compliance with state and federal laws, including but not limited to Title XII, Title IX, and the ADA. E-Verify, EOE. Apply Now NWU Facebook NWU X NWU Instagram NWU YouTube NWU LinkedIn Apply Schedule a Visit Request Information Donate Title IX Non-discrimination Privacy Policy Report a Concern Digital accessibility Contact Us 5000 Saint Paul Avenue Lincoln, NE 68504-2794 (402) 466-2371 Experiences that change you"
